{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball","id":1484299,"title":"Net successes add to the damage of the \"Fireball\"?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-17T15:11:10-07:00","id":1484299,"title":"Net successes add to the damage of the \"Fireball\"?","content":"So, in a heated discussion with a friend, we came upon this subject. If a Mage uses his Forces + Prime to throw a fireball (or any other magical attack, it's just that the fabled fireball is a well known example) against his enemy, do you have your mage roll to hit and, if so, do the net successes add to the final damage? My take is yes, but my French friend thinks the damage should only come from the damage table for damage. What's your opinion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T16:55:40-07:00","id":1484312,"title":"","content":"I don't quite remember is there's a clear answer in the books, if anyone can help me, I'd be glad!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T17:16:23-07:00","id":1484314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball#post1484299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in a heated discussion with a friend, we came upon this subject. If a Mage uses his Forces + Prime to throw a fireball (or any other magical attack, it's just that the fabled fireball is a well known example) against his enemy, do you have your mage roll to hit and, if so, do the net successes add to the final damage? My take is yes, but my French friend thinks the damage should only come from the damage table for damage. What's your opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it were Forces alone, it would be an instantaneous effect, like your friend suggested. If the combined Prime (2) + Forces effect were cast as a whole-round-action, it would be spell damage. If you create the fireball, ahead of using it, you have on &quot;object&quot; of a sort that can be wielded, if the storyteller deems that the mages practice lines up with such wielding. I would certainly suggest wearing fire-retardant gloves. If not, push it around with further Forces effects or concentration. <br /> <br /> Adding life 3, you could anchor it to the target's pattern, fire and forget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T18:05:40-07:00","id":1484317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484314#post1484314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it were Forces alone, it would be an instantaneous effect, like your friend suggested. If the combined Prime (2) + Forces effect were cast as a whole-round-action, it would be spell damage. If you create the fireball, ahead of using it, you have on &amp;quot;object&amp;quot; of a sort that can be wielded, if the storyteller deems that the mages practice lines up with such wielding. I would certainly suggest wearing fire-retardant gloves. If not, push it around with further Forces effects or concentration. <br /> <br /> Adding life 3, you could anchor it to the target's pattern, fire and forget.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why Life 3? Life 1 is already &quot;Detect Life&quot;. If your effect is &quot;Forces 3 moving object to target detected with Life&quot; that's Life 1, not 3.<br /> <br /> And, if you analyzed the target's aura with Prime 1, you can do just the same, but instead of a fixed Life Pattern, you guide it to the aura that you fix. Since it's already using Prime 2, you can just do it in a single effect - if you first analyze the aura, without needing another Sphere.<br /> <br /> Oh, ok, now I understood the whole concept. I remember (vaguely) that in 2E had something like that, that you add successes to &quot;hit&quot;, but in 3E (revised) there were no such a thing, it was just 2x the successes (+1 for Forces). So, you had to spend 1 success for target (so 1 success for a single target), and the rest multiply x2 and add a +1 to the damage.<br /> <br /> Now, for M20 I really dont remember. But after Revised there was no such a thing as successes adding damage, nor there was any difference betwenn being a single Sphere, or just Forces, or Forces + Prime, or Life 3 or Entropy 4 or any other, except that Forces give a +1 on top of it all.<br /> <br /> At least that's as far as I remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T18:59:21-07:00","id":1484321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484317#post1484317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why Life 3? Life 1 is already &quot;Detect Life&quot;. If your effect is &quot;Forces 3 moving object to target detected with Life&quot; that's Life 1, not 3.<br /> <br /> And, if you analyzed the target's aura with Prime 1, you can do just the same, but instead of a fixed Life Pattern, you guide it to the aura that you fix. Since it's already using Prime 2, you can just do it in a single effect - if you first analyze the aura, without needing another Sphere.<br /> <br /> Oh, ok, now I understood the whole concept. I remember (vaguely) that in 2E had something like that, that you add successes to &quot;hit&quot;, but in 3E (revised) there were no such a thing, it was just 2x the successes (+1 for Forces). So, you had to spend 1 success for target (so 1 success for a single target), and the rest multiply x2 and add a +1 to the damage.<br /> <br /> Now, for M20 I really dont remember. But after Revised there was no such a thing as successes adding damage, nor there was any difference betwenn being a single Sphere, or just Forces, or Forces + Prime, or Life 3 or Entropy 4 or any other, except that Forces give a +1 on top of it all.<br /> <br /> At least that's as far as I remember.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In general every attack get net successes to the damage based on how many successes you have above the enemy (that is, if he attempt to dodge), if he doesn't attempt to dodge you just have to &quot;spend&quot; 1 success to hit and the rest of the net successes is added to the damage. That's what I mean. Just one small correction here, Forces add 1 success to the table, not a single 1 of damage. So if the guy has 5 successes with a fireball attack (here we go, fireball again...) it would cause 10 damage, but as forces adds 1 success, it becomes 6 successes which translates into whooping 18 of damage, i.e. successes x3 damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T19:12:40-07:00","id":1484322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484317#post1484317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why Life 3? Life 1 is already &quot;Detect Life&quot;. If your effect is &quot;Forces 3 moving object to target detected with Life&quot; that's Life 1, not 3.<br /> <br /> And, if you analyzed the target's aura with Prime 1, you can do just the same, but instead of a fixed Life Pattern, you guide it to the aura that you fix. Since it's already using Prime 2, you can just do it in a single effect - if you first analyze the aura, without needing another Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I suggested is a Prime 2, Life 3, Forces 3 effect. You use both Life and Prime to anchor the Forces effect to the target. The advantage to this is that they <i>keep burning</i>. If the target can't unweave the spell, they are toast.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T23:26:58-07:00","id":1484330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484321#post1484321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In general every attack get net successes to the damage based on how many successes you have above the enemy (that is, if he attempt to dodge), if he doesn't attempt to dodge you just have to &amp;quot;spend&amp;quot; 1 success to hit and the rest of the net successes is added to the damage. That's what I mean. Just one small correction here, Forces add 1 success to the table, not a single 1 of damage. So if the guy has 5 successes with a fireball attack (here we go, fireball again...) it would cause 10 damage, but as forces adds 1 success, it becomes 6 successes which translates into whooping 18 of damage, i.e. successes x3 damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the part of the difference in editions I was talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T15:41:10-07:00","id":1484391,"title":"","content":"You can go both ways.<br /> <br /> If you're hurling the Fireball as a thrown weapon, it is a thrown weapon. You need to make the spell in such a way as for the fireball to behave like that. Then, by all means, you would add successes in the throw to the damage. You basically constructed a weapon and used it.<br /> <br /> But if you're just using your spell (and this single action), then you're not making an attack, you're just creating an effect. In that case there may be any number of ways for either you to aim it or the target to dodge it, but probably adding something to &quot;lock&quot; the target would be good. And I would probably default to the target having to dodge against your spell instead of a hitting roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T17:24:27-07:00","id":1484401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484322#post1484322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I suggested is a Prime 2, Life 3, Forces 3 effect. You use both Life and Prime to anchor the Forces effect to the target. The advantage to this is that they <i>keep burning</i>. If the target can't unweave the spell, they are toast.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could still probably get away with sticking to prime only for the same effect. It'd need prime 3, but the spell would anchor to the targets unique aura and use the target's own quintessence to empower itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T17:38:30-07:00","id":1484403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484401#post1484401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could still probably get away with sticking to prime only for the same effect. It'd need prime 3, but the spell would anchor to the targets unique aura and use the target's own quintessence to empower itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the aura a &quot;thing&quot; you can attach material effects to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T19:05:50-07:00","id":1484407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484403#post1484403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the aura a &quot;thing&quot; you can attach material effects to?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to attach the effect, just imbue the spell with the targeting. Any Perception effect would render the spell itself able to home at least on something you can magically perceive at the time of casting, and Prime auras still have a spatial location.<br /> <br /> The best option would certainly be Correspondence for any homing effect, but with a visual of the target it isn't needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T02:27:54-07:00","id":1484490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484401#post1484401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and use the target's own quintessence to empower itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a Prime 5 effect not Prime 3 - draining quintessence from a living being (V20 p521)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T03:05:42-07:00","id":1484493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484490#post1484490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a Prime 5 effect not Prime 3 - draining quintessence from a living being (<b>V20</b> p521)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mean Mage 20<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20, Page 521</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Prime</b> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Channel Quintessence/ Enchant Life/ Energy Weapon/ Craft Periapts &amp; Temporary Wonders</b><br /> <br /> By tapping into the flow of Quintessence around her, the Prime-skilled mage can draw both free and raw Quintessence from Nodes, Junctures (special times), and Tass (solidified Quintessence)\u2026 and she may also channel that energy into new and existing Patterns as well. With such powers, she could (with Life 3) enchant a living thing so that it could inflict or endure aggravated damage; <b>inflict aggravated damage by shaking up that organism\u2019s life force; pull small amounts of life force from a living sacrifice or (with Matter 2) from inert objects;</b> instill Quintessence into a vessel called a Periapt; or \u2013 with other Spheres \u2013 craft temporary Talismans or Devices by infusing them with Primal Force. (Permanent enchantments require Prime 4 \u2013 see Crafting Wonders on p. 508, and Quintessence Amounts on p. 507.) In desperate circumstances, a Prime-schooled mage can also create temporary weapons out of pure concentrated energy \u2013 blasts of Quintessence or swords of light. Such weapons inflict aggravated damage (as per the Base Damage or Durationchart) and cost one point of Quintessence per use\u2026 or, for weapons that last for a length of time, one point per turn. When the mage runs of out Quintessence, the weapon disappears. Unless channeled through energy-guns or conjured as miracles among the faithful, such attacks are inevitably vulgar.</div> </div> </div> </div>You only need prime 3 to pull life force as quintessence for an effect, you don't even need the life sphere to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T06:30:53-07:00","id":1484507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484493#post1484493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You only need prime 3 to pull life force as quintessence for an effect, you don't even need the life sphere to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pulling from a sacrifice isn't the same as pulling as a part of the effect, and Prime 5 does make it clear as only then it is stated the possibility of unraveling a Pattern as part of the effect and getting the Quint in the process.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'll squarely side with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11490_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11490\" data-vbnamecard=\"11490\">Dogstar</a> here, reading in this that you can use the target's own Quint against them is clearly stretching things well beyond reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T06:34:34-07:00","id":1484508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484493#post1484493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you mean Mage 20<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <br /> You only need prime 3 to pull life force as quintessence for an effect, you don't even need the life sphere to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did, well spotted.<br /> <br /> Interestingly I've been having a discussion with my group about this today. The description under Prime 3 specifies <b>'life force'</b> rather than quintessence. I was rather perplexed until I re-read the Energy-Work chapter in How Do you Do That, specifically around p49. There's a section on 'Harvesting Quintessence Through Sacrifice' - but it's an <b>optional</b> rule. So it seems that the use of the phrase 'life force' was quite deliberate and allows for two different interpretations.<br /> <br /> Without the optional rule 'life force' seems to refer to health levels rather than quintessence (there's a section immediately before discussing adding health levels)<br /> <br /> However with the optional rule in place 'life force' means either health levels and/or quintessence. So you can harvest quintessence from destroying objects and from willing sacrifices at prime 3 (there are further notes about unwilling sacrifices and the problems with that)<br /> <br /> I think this is one of the major changes between earlier editions and M20 - the approach to quintessence and it's rarity. That optional rule allows you to move a touch closer to the previous versions and makes quintessence more available than 'by the book' M20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 06-20-2022, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T09:45:26-07:00","id":1484516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484507#post1484507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pulling from a sacrifice isn't the same as pulling as a part of the effect, and Prime 5 does make it clear as only then it is stated the possibility of unraveling a Pattern as part of the effect and getting the Quint in the process.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'll squarely side with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11490_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11490\" data-vbnamecard=\"11490\">Dogstar</a> here, reading in this that you can use the target's own Quint against them is clearly stretching things well beyond reason.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484508#post1484508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did, well spotted.<br /> <br /> Interestingly I've been having a discussion with my group about this today. The description under Prime 3 specifies <b>'life force'</b> rather than quintessence. I was rather perplexed until I re-read the Energy-Work chapter in How Do you Do That, specifically around p49. There's a section on 'Harvesting Quintessence Through Sacrifice' - but it's an <b>optional</b> rule. So it seems that the use of the phrase 'life force' was quite deliberate and allows for two different interpretations.<br /> <br /> Without the optional rule 'life force' seems to refer to health levels rather than quintessence (there's a section immediately before discussing adding health levels)<br /> <br /> However with the optional rule in place 'life force' means either health levels and/or quintessence. So you can harvest quintessence from destroying objects and from willing sacrifices at prime 3 (there are further notes about unwilling sacrifices and the problems with that)<br /> <br /> I think this is one of the major changes between earlier editions and M20 - the approach to quintessence and it's rarity. That optional rule allows you to move a touch closer to the previous versions and makes quintessence more available than 'by the book' M20</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I didn't know they made that an optional rule in M20. In previous editions prime 3 let you steal Quintessence from something you Damaged/Destroyed. A prime 3 mage could alter a spell made with another sphere to steal quintessence from something in proportion to the damage it did.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T03:33:09-07:00","id":1484597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1484299-net-successes-add-to-the-damage-of-the-fireball?p=1484516#post1484516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Huh, I didn't know they made that an optional rule in M20. In previous editions prime 3 let you steal Quintessence from something you Damaged/Destroyed. A prime 3 mage could alter a spell made with another sphere to steal quintessence from something in proportion to the damage it did.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well you still can, provided that your group agrees to the optional rule, and that the spell is worked well enough, because sacrificing an unwilling victim for their quintessence is still doable but wrapping several effects into a single spell should get you some sort of difficulty increase or require multiple castings or something 'extra' as it's otherwise an extremely dangerous combination to allow. The spell above used it's victim's quintessence to power the spell so that's at least three 'effects': a damage effect, a quintessence drain effect, and a quintessence transfer/channelling effect<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 06-21-2022, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}